// BLS wrapper reads, writes and comparisons under the legacy and basic
// schemes.
//
// eager: the outcome of reading each input under each scheme. "throw"
// for bytes canonical under neither scheme, "invalid" for the invalid
// object, which encodes as zeros, and "valid" for an object that encodes
// back to the input. A valid object's encoding under the other scheme is
// legacy_to_basic or basic_to_legacy. A class ending in _basic writes the
// first input of another class in the basic layout, and one ending in
// _neg flips the legacy sign bit of the first input of another class.
//
// lazy: runs of [script, the output of each operation after the first]
// on a lazy object read from the class's first input. The first operation
// builds the object: unser:S reads the input under S, new:S is the default
// object made under S, and set:XY sets the object a lazy read under X
// gives, with scheme Y. ser writes under the object's scheme, ser:S under
// S, hash hashes what ser writes, get decodes, legacy:S sets the scheme,
// islegacy gives it, and copy continues on a copy. Written bytes are
// tags: raw for the input, zero, or XY for the valid object the eager
// read under X gives, written under Y; h:<tag> is the double SHA-256 of a
// tagged string. get gives invalid, valid:X for the object the eager read
// under X gives, or the legacy and basic encodings. Untagged bytes are
// hex, and - marks no output.
//
// pairs: a and b are [class, script] for two lazy objects, and eq gives
// whether a == b, then what a and b write afterwards, as tags of their own
// inputs. b == a gives the same.
//
// Inputs come from pkgs/pkc/contrib/gen_wrapper.cpp, seed 0x3a77e5, up to 3
// per class, and outcomes from the BLS wrapper of the release the dash
// submodule pins. Regenerate with pkgs/pkc/contrib/regen.py.
